1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,950
If you scratch your legs every night,

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:04,170
it isn't only because you skip moisturizer.

3
00:00:05,570 --> 00:00:09,480
At night, skin temperature rises and
cortisol falls, so the itch gets worse.

4
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:14,280
If the front of your shins cracks and
turns white, that's dry-skin eczema.

5
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:18,840
Dry air from indoor heating and
frequent bathing make it worse.

6
00:00:20,350 --> 00:00:24,360
If the insides of your elbows and knees
keep turning red, that's atopic dermatitis.

7
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:27,910
The itch comes first,
and the rash follows.

8
00:00:29,370 --> 00:00:31,730
Topical steroids are not
the same as steroid pills.

9
00:00:33,070 --> 00:00:34,890
On the face, use a mild strength
for a short time;

10
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:38,700
on the trunk and limbs, a medium strength,
only for as long as it's needed.

11
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:43,190
Before bed, apply moisturizer once more
to your shins and arms,

12
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:46,150
and use a blanket just warm enough
that you feel a light sweat.
